  "claim": "The village and civil parish where Harold Temple White was born is in North East Lincolnshire, England. It is 1.75 miles east from the place the River Freshney, according to folk lore, springs from.",
  "evidencia": "Page: Welbeck Hill. Sentence: Welbeck Hill is the site of Roman and early Saxon pottery finds, and an Anglo-Saxon cemetery, located around 1.75 miles from Laceby, and around 3 miles from Riby, in North East Lincolnshire, England.\nPage: Laceby. Sentence: Laceby is a village and civil parish in North East Lincolnshire, England.\nPage: River Freshney. Sentence: It rises from at least four springs on the edge of the Lincolnshire Wolds, although local folklore and oral tradition has it springing from Welbeck Hill.\nPage: Harold Temple White. Sentence: He was born in Laceby, Lincolnshire, England, in 1881, and resided in Wellington for much of his life.",
