        "id": 0,
        "original_id": "3ab23f74-3e31-5d5f-ab84-5b089371a9d9",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- Places: Welbeck Hill, Laceby, Riby, North East Lincolnshire, England, Lincolnshire Wolds, Wellington\n- People: Harold Temple White\n- Topics: Roman pottery, early Saxon pottery, Anglo-Saxon cemetery, River Freshney, local folklore, oral tradition\n\nFacts:\n- Welbeck Hill is located about 1.75 miles from Laceby and about 3 miles from Riby in North East Lincolnshire, England.\n- Welbeck Hill is the site of Roman and early Saxon pottery finds and an Anglo-Saxon cemetery.\n- Laceby is a village and civil parish in North East Lincolnshire, England.\n- River Freshney rises from at least four springs on the edge of the Lincolnshire Wolds.\n- Local folklore and oral tradition say that River Freshney springs from Welbeck Hill.\n- Harold Temple White was born in Laceby, Lincolnshire, England, in 1881.\n- Harold Temple White resided in Wellington for much of his life.",
        "type": "TextSummary"
      },
      {
        "id": 1,
        "original_id": "13b1c919-7d64-5727-a1b8-8aa2d15b848c",
